<body lang=3D"en-SE" link=3D"blue" vlink=3D"purple" style=3D"word-wrap:brea=
k-word">
<div class=3D"WordSection1">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US">Muhammad Usama Sardar wrote:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US">&gt;Do we have an I-D which defines how long do we consider as long=
-term connections? or I-D which gives recommendations or best practices for=
 how long do we consider TLS 1.3 to provide
 excellent security?<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">- One clear timepoint is when the server certicate ex=
pire</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso=
-fareast-language:EN-US">s</span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#007=
0C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">.
 TLS 1.3 removed the ability to do server reauthentication. <o:p></o:p></sp=
an></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">- RFC 4253 recommends rekeying with PFS after each gi=
gabyte of transmitted data or after each hour of connection time.<o:p></o:p=
></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">- French ANSSI recommends periodic rekeying with PFS,=
 e.g. every hour and every 100 GB of data, in order to limit the impact of =
a key compromise.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US"><a href=3D"https://cyber.gouv.fr/sites/default/files/=
2015/09/NT_IPsec_EN.pdf">https://cyber.gouv.fr/sites/default/files/2015/09/=
NT_IPsec_EN.pdf</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">- The chief cryptographer of the Swedish NCSA states =
that asymmetrically distributed key</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"fon=
t-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">s</span><span style=
=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">
 can be refreshed at very frequent intervals and that options include conti=
nuously re-negotiating the encryption keys, and chaining the negotiations, =
so that the adversary has to record and store an uninterrupted sequence of =
negotiations, and then break them
 in sequence.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US"><a href=3D"http://kth.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2=
:1902626/FULLTEXT01.pdf">http://kth.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1902626=
/FULLTEXT01.pdf</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"SV" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0=
070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">So 1 hour</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-si=
ze:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">,
</span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:E=
N-US">1-100 GB</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#=
0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">, or</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D=
"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">
</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-far=
east-language:EN-US">server cert expiry date,
</span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:E=
N-US">whichever comes sooner? You could also arguee that with blazingly fas=
t algorithms like X25519 and ML-KEM and much faster hardware, best practice=
 have changed since 2006 and excellent
 security is </span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0=
070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">now a</span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0=
pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">symmetric</span><span style=3D=
"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">
<span lang=3D"EN-US">rekeying at </span></span><span style=3D"font-size:11.=
0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">very frequent intervals with =
chaining</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0=
;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">, this is e.g.,
 what Signal does.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US">&gt;If the intention of draft was #2 above, cross-reading with this=
 sentence, are we implying that PQC is not an urgent security issue?
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">That is a very good point. I suggest changing this to=
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">OLD: =93This document specifies that outside of urgen=
t security fixes, no new features will be approved for TLS 1.2=94<o:p></o:p=
></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">NEW: =93This document specifies that, no new features=
 will be approved for TLS 1.2=94<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">(TLS WG can always make a future RFC overriding this =
anyway=85)<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US">&gt;It looks like a more detailed version of tls12-frozen draft. Is=
 there a good reason not to merge the two documents?<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">I had the same thought. I think they would be better =
as a single document. But I don=92t care very much.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US">&gt;What does the capitalization of WILL NOT mean?
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US">Yes, and it is not in RFC 6919 either=85</span><span =
style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">
<span lang=3D"EN-US">;)<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0;mso-fa=
reast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"SV" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0=
070C0;mso-fareast-language:EN-US">Cheers,<br>
John<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<div id=3D"mail-editor-reference-message-container">
<div>
<div>
<div style=3D"border:none;border-top:solid #B5C4DF 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm =
0cm 0cm">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt"><b><span style=3D"col=
or:black">From:
</span></b><span style=3D"color:black">Muhammad Usama Sardar &lt;muhammad_u=
sama.sardar@tu-dresden.de&gt;<br>
<b>Date: </b>Friday, 6 December 2024 at 18:33<br>
<b>To: </b>Valery Smyslov &lt;smyslov.ietf@gmail.com&gt;, 'Sean Turner' &lt=
;sean@sn3rd.com&gt;, 'TLS List' &lt;tls@ietf.org&gt;<br>
<b>Subject: </b>[TLS] Re: Working Group Last Call for TLS 1.2 is in Feature=
 Freeze<o:p></o:p></span></p>
</div>
<p>A few quick questions. Sorry if I am missing something obvious or some b=
ackground.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">On 04.12.24 08:04, Valery Smyslov wrote: <o:p></o:p>=
</p>
<blockquote style=3D"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt">
<pre>note, that UTA WG has issued a WGLC for draft-ietf-uta-require-tls13-0=
2 (New Protocols Must Require TLS 1.3) [1].<o:p></o:p></pre>
<pre><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></pre>
<pre> [1] <a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-uta-requir=
e-tls13/">https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-uta-require-tls13/</a=
><o:p></o:p></pre>
</blockquote>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Thanks for pointer to this. It looks like a more det=
ailed version of tls12-frozen draft. Is there a good reason not to merge th=
e two documents? Is it due to different WGs? or different intended status? =
or something else?
<o:p></o:p></p>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">On 04.12.24 10:36, John Mattsson wrote:<o:p></o:p></=
p>
</div>
<blockquote style=3D"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-a=
lt:auto"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">as-is, TLS 1.3 does not provide e=
xcellent security for long-term connections.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Do we have an I-D which defines <i>how long</i> do we consider as long-t=
erm connections? or I-D which gives recommendations or best practices for
<i>how long </i>do we consider TLS 1.3 to provide excellent security?<o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p>---<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>Considering the following two statements in I-D, I have two questions: <=
o:p></o:p></p>
<pre style=3D"background:white;box-sizing:border-box;white-space:pre-wrap;f=
ont-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;orphans:2;text-align:=
start;widows:2;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;=
overflow:auto;word-spacing:0px"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;color:#2125=
29">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; For TLS it is important to note that the focus of thes=
e efforts is<o:p></o:p></span></pre>
<pre style=3D"background:white"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;color:#2125=
29">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; TLS 1.3 or later.&nbsp; Put bluntly, post-quantum cryp=
tography for TLS 1.2<o:p></o:p></span></pre>
<pre style=3D"background:white"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;color:#2125=
29">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; WILL NOT be supported.<o:p></o:p></span></pre>
<p>To me the two sentences are contradicting. Which one of the following is=
 intended?
<o:p></o:p></p>
<ol start=3D"1" type=3D"1">
<li class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-=
alt:auto;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1">
(My understanding from 1st sentence) Some PQC support for TLS 1.2 will stil=
l continue but it will not be the focus.&nbsp;
<o:p></o:p></li><li class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;ms=
o-margin-bottom-alt:auto;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1">
(My understanding from 2nd sentence) We will exclusively work on PQC for TL=
S 1.3 or later.
<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<p>What does the capitalization of WILL NOT mean? I did not find any such c=
apitalization in RFC 2119 and RFC 8174. Please add the relevant RFC in sect=
ion 2 or define it.
<o:p></o:p></p>
<pre style=3D"background:white;box-sizing:border-box;white-space:pre-wrap;f=
ont-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;orphans:2;text-align:=
start;widows:2;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;=
overflow:auto;word-spacing:0px"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;color:#2125=
29">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; This<o:p></o:p></span></pre>
<pre style=3D"background:white"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;color:#2125=
29">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; document specifies that outside of urgent security fix=
es, no new<o:p></o:p></span></pre>
<pre style=3D"background:white"><span style=3D"font-size:10.5pt;color:#2125=
29">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; features will be approved for TLS 1.2.<o:p></o:p></spa=
n></pre>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">If the intention of draft was #2 above, cross-readin=
g with this sentence, are we implying that PQC is not an urgent security is=
sue?
<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>

--_000_GVXPR07MB9678AE6A1DD7953668BE73DF89322GVXPR07MB9678eurp_--

